  {
   "q": "Apply Tkinter to create a basic event-driven GUI where a button displays a message when clicked.",
   "answer": [
    "from tkinter import *",
    "def show_message(): label.config(text=\"Hello, Tkinter!\")",
    "window = Tk() window.title(\"Event Demo\")",
    "label = Label(window, text=\"\") label.pack()",
    "button = Button(window, text=\"Click Me\", command=show_message) button.pack()",
    "window.mainloop()",
    "This GUI reacts to user interaction via an event (button click), demonstrating core event-driven principles of input handling and dynamic output."
